#: ../doc/timeline.rst:23
msgid "Timeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:25
msgid "The timeline is where your video comes together. You arrange clips, trim them, layer visuals, and make timing decisions here. If you are new to editing, think of the timeline as a simple left-to-right story: earlier moments on the left, later moments on the right."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:32
msgid "If you are just getting started, read :ref:`quick_tutorial_ref` first, then come back here for more detail. For a labeled breakdown of toolbar controls, see :ref:`timeline_toolbar_ref`. To select, move, and trim clips and transitions with the keyboard, see :ref:`timeline_keyboard_ref`. You can also focus Project Files with :kbd:`Shift+1` and press :kbd:`Ctrl+Enter` to place selected files at the playhead on the target track."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:40
msgid "Timeline Basics"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:42
msgid "These terms are used often in this guide:"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:48
msgid "Term"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:48
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:50
msgid "Playhead"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:50
msgid "The red line that shows your current time position."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:51
msgid "Track"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:51
msgid "A horizontal layer that holds clips (top tracks appear above lower tracks)."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:52
msgid "Clip"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:52
msgid "A video, audio, or image item placed on a track."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:53
msgid "Transition"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:53
msgid "A blend between two overlapping clips."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:54
msgid "Marker"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:54
msgid "A saved point in time you can jump back to quickly."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:55
msgid "Keyframe"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:55
msgid "A saved value at a point in time (used for animation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:58
msgid "For a full glossary, see :ref:`glossary_ref`."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:61
msgid "Current Timecode"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:63
msgid "The current timecode appears at the left side of the timeline ruler and shows the playhead's exact position. Click the timecode, enter a new value, and press :kbd:`Enter` to move the playhead to that frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:67
msgid "Clear the field or enter ``0`` to jump to the start of the timeline. Press :kbd:`Up` or :kbd:`Down` to step the selected timecode segment; hold :kbd:`Shift` to step by 10. When the frame segment is selected, hold :kbd:`Ctrl` to step by one second. Press :kbd:`Esc` to cancel."
msgstr ""

