#: ../doc/timeline.rst:87
msgid "Selecting Clips and Transitions"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:89
msgid "Selection is one of the most important timeline skills:"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:91
msgid "Click an item to select it."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:92
msgid ":kbd:`Ctrl+Click` adds or removes items from selection."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:93
msgid ":kbd:`Shift+Click` selects a range between your anchor item and the clicked item."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:94
msgid ":kbd:`Ctrl+Shift+Click` adds that range to your current selection."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:95
msgid ":kbd:`Alt+Click` ripple-selects from the clicked item to the end of the track."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:96
msgid "Drag an empty-area selection box to select multiple items."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:98
msgid "See :ref:`clips_ref` for the full list and examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:101
msgid "Timeline Toolbar and Zoom"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:103
msgid "The timeline toolbar helps with common navigation and editing actions (snapping, auto keyframes, retime, razor, markers, centering, and zoom)."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:106
msgid "Use the diamond button to turn :ref:`auto_keyframes_ref` on or off. Leave it on to build animations as you edit, or turn it off to adjust existing values without adding keyframes."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:109
msgid "The :ref:`razor_tool_ref` shows a cut guide and timecode over the target clip. While paused, hovering also previews the cut frame without moving the playhead. Click to cut, or press :kbd:`Esc` to leave Razor mode. The Razor guide respects the existing **Snapping** toggle and uses the same snap targets and tolerance as other timeline edits."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:115
msgid "Tip: If timeline editing feels crowded, zoom in with the timeline slider to make small clip adjustments easier."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:118
msgid "You can also zoom the timeline with :kbd:`Ctrl+Scroll Wheel`. On the QWidget timeline, hold :kbd:`Ctrl` and drag with the middle mouse button for smooth zooming."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:123
msgid "Tracks, Locking, and Inserting"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:125
msgid "Tracks help organize your edit. A common setup is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:127
msgid "Top tracks: titles, overlays, logos, picture-in-picture"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:128
msgid "Middle tracks: main video content"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:129
msgid "Lower tracks: music and sound effects"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:131
msgid "You can lock tracks to protect them from accidental edits and use insert/ripple editing when you need later clips to move automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:134
msgid "For track layout basics, see :ref:`tracks_ref`. For detailed clip editing behavior, see :ref:`clips_cutting_slicing_ref`."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/timeline.rst:138
msgid "For projects with many layers, choose **Minimal** or **Compact** under **Preferences → Timeline → Track Size** to see more tracks with less scrolling. Choose **Relaxed** for more vertical room, or **Default** to restore the theme's original height. Keyframe panel spacing adjusts too. See :ref:`preferences_track_size_ref` for details."
msgstr ""

